          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The modern picture of effective low-energy QFT goes back to
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                L. P. Kadanoff,
                %em
                  Scaling laws for Ising models near
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_c
                , Physica 2 (1966);
            %li#Wilson71
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+Wilson"}> Kenneth Wilson
                ,
                %em Renormalization group and critical phenomena 1. Renormalization group and the Kadanoff scaling picture
                , , Physical review B 4(9) (1971) (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.4.3174"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.4.3174
                )
            %li#Wilson71b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+Wilson"}> Kenneth Wilson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Renormalization group and critical phenomena. 2. Phase space cell analysis of critical behavior
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.4.3184"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.4.3184
            %li#Weinberg79
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Weinberg"}> Steven Weinberg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Phenomenological Lagrangians
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0378-4371(79)90223-1"} doi:10.1016/0378-4371(79)90223-1
            %li#Polchinski84
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Polchinski"}> Joseph Polchinski
                ,
                %em Renormalization and effective Lagrangians
                , Nuclear Phys. B B231, 1984 (
                %a{:href => "http://max2.physics.sunysb.edu/~rastelli/2016/Polchinski.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Leutwyler94
              %p H. Leutwyler, Ann. Phys., NY 235 (1994) 165.
          %p Early history:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Weinberg"}> Steven Weinberg
              ,
              %em On the Development of Effective Field Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.04241"}> arXiv:2101.04241
              )
          %p
            The point that perturbatively
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} non-renormalizable
            theories may be regarded as effective field theories at each energy scale was highligted in
          %ul
            %li#GomisWeinberg95
              J. Gomis,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Weinberg"} Steven Weinberg
              = succeed "," do
                %em Are nonrenormalizable gauge theories renormalizable?
              %strong 469
              (1996) 473 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9510087"}> arXiv:hep-th/9510087
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li#Weinberg09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Weinberg"}> Steven Weinberg
                ,
                %em Effective Field Theory, Past and Future
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0908.1964"}> arXiv:0908.1964
                )
            %li#Pich
              %p
                A. Pich,
                %em Effective Field Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/9806303"}> arXiv:hep-ph/9806303
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                , Lecture 5 of:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Five+lectures+on+supersymmetry"} Five lectures on supersymmetry
                (1999)
            %li#Abdesselam13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Abdelmalek+Abdesselam"}> Abdelmalek Abdesselam
                ,
                %em QFT, RG, and all that, for mathematicians, in eleven pages
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.4897"}> arXiv:1311.4897
                )
            %li
              %p
                Andrey Grozin,
                %em Effective field theories
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.00434"}> arXiv:2001.00434
                )
            %li
              %p
                Riccardo Penco,
                %em An Introduction to Effective Field Theories
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.16285"}> arXiv:2006.16285
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adam+Falkowski"}> Adam Falkowski
                , Christoph Bobeth:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on Effective Field Theories
                %a{:href => "https://indico.in2p3.fr/event/22195/"} GDR-Intensity Frontier lectures
                (2020) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://indico.in2p3.fr/event/22195/#21-lecture-4-introduction-to-s"}> webpage
                , script:
                %a{:href => "https://indico.in2p3.fr/event/22195/contributions/86017/attachments/59873/81148/eftlectures.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cliff+P.+Burgess"}> Cliff P. Burgess
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to effective field theory
                %strong 57
                (2007) 329-362 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0701053"}> arXiv:hep-th/0701053
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev.nucl.56.080805.140508"} doi:10.1146/annurev.nucl.56.080805.140508
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cliff+P.+Burgess"}> Cliff P. Burgess
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to effective field theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/introduction-to-effective-field-theory/A9CDB35F4AA7921E3A9CFD573EBA8B64"} ISBN:9781139048040
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://physics.mcmaster.ca/~cburgess/Book/Ch1-6SnippetEFT.pdf"} pdf
          %p A classical textbook adopting the EFT perspective:
          %ul
            %li#Weinberg95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Weinberg"}> Steven Weinberg
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Quantum Theory of Fields Vol 1: Foundations
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139644167"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781139644167
            %li#Weinberg96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Weinberg"}> Steven Weinberg
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Quantum Theory of Fields Vol 2: Applications
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139644174"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781139644174
          %p whose author describes his goal as:
          %blockquote
            %p “This is intended to be a book on quantum field theory for the era of effective field theory.”
          %p Another QFT textbook book which takes the effective-field-theory approach:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anthony+Zee"}> Anthony Zee
              ,
              %em Quantum Field Theory in a Nutshell
              (Princeton University Press, second edition, 2010).
          %p
            On effective field theory for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneously+broken+symmetries"} spontaneously broken symmetries
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom%C3%A1%C5%A1+Brauner"}> Tomáš Brauner
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Effective Field Theory for Spontaneously Broken Symmetry
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 1023
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.14518"} arXiv:2404.14518
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-48378-3"} doi:10.1007/978-3-031-48378-3
          %p
            On effective field theory for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+quantum+systems"} open quantum systems
            with application to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmology"} cosmology
          %ul
            %li
              Thomas Colas:
              %em Lectures on Open Effective Field Theories
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.00140"}> arXiv:2510.00140
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#ReferencesInCausalPerturbationTheory Via causal perturbation theory
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+QFT"} perturbative
            effective QFT in the rigorous context of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+AQFT"} perturbative AQFT
            and its relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/St%C3%BCckelberg-Petermann+renormalization+group"} Stückelberg-Petermann renormalization group
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#BrunettiDuetschFredenhagen09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Romeo+Brunetti"}> Romeo Brunetti
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+D%C3%BCtsch"} Michael Dütsch
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Perturbative Algebraic Quantum Field Theory and the Renormalization Groups
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0901.2038"} arXiv:0901.2038
            %li#Duetsch10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+D%C3%BCtsch"}> Michael Dütsch
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Connection between the renormalization groups of Stückelberg-Petermann and Wilson
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1012.5604"} arXiv:1012.5604
            %li#DuetschFredenhagenKellerRejzner14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+D%C3%BCtsch"}> Michael Dütsch
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kai+Keller"} Kai Keller
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Katarzyna+Rejzner"} Katarzyna Rejzner
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dimensional Regularization in Position Space, and a Forest Formula for Epstein-Glaser Renormalization
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.5424"} arXiv:1311.5424
          %p reviewed in
          %ul
            %li#Duetsch18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+D%C3%BCtsch"}> Michael Dütsch
              , section 3.8 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/From+classical+field+theory+to+perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} From classical field theory to perturbative quantum field theory
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#KellerKopperSchophaus97
              Georg Keller, Christoph Kopper, Clemens Schophaus,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Perturbative Renormalization with Flow Equations in Minkowski Space
              %strong 70
              (1997) 247-274 (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9605137"}> arXiv.hep-th/9605137
              )
          %h3#for_nuclear_physics_2 For nuclear physics
          %p
            Discussion for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nuclear+physics"} nuclear physics
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mannque+Rho"}> Mannque Rho
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lectures on Effective Field Theories for Nuclei, Nuclear Matter and Dense Matter
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/nucl-th/0202078"} arXiv:nucl-th/0202078
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://cds.cern.ch/record/539674"} cds:539674
          %h3#for_condensed_matter_physics For condensed matter physics
          %p
            Discussion of effective field theories in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+matter+theory"} condensed matter theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+state+physics"} solid state physics
            \:
          %ul
            %li#Shankar99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ramamurti+Shankar"}> Ramamurti Shankar
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Effective Field Theory in Condensed Matter Physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conceptual Foundations of Quantum Field Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/9703210"} arXiv:cond-mat/9703210
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511470813.007"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511470813.007
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eduardo+Fradkin"}> Eduardo Fradkin
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Field Theories of Condensed Matter Physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139015509"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781139015509
            %li
              %p
                Eduardo C. Marino,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Field Theory Approach to Condensed Matter Physics
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781139696548"} doi:10.1017/9781139696548
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom%C3%A1%C5%A1+Brauner"}> Tomáš Brauner
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sean+A.+Hartnoll"} Sean A. Hartnoll
                et al:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Snowmass White Paper: Effective Field Theories for Condensed Matter Systems
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/conferences/1803127"} Snowmass 2021
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.10110"}> arXiv:2203.10110
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/2055714"} inSpire:2055714
          %h3#for_particle_physics For particle physics
          %p
            Discussion for (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model
            of)
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particle+physics"} particle physics
          %ul
            %li#PetrovBlechman16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexey+Petrov"}> Alexey Petrov
              , Andrew E Blechman,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Effective Field Theories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/8619"} doi:10.1142/8619
          %h3#for_gravity For gravity
          %p
            Notably the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            based on the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Hilbert+action"} Einstein-Hilbert action
            may be regarded as just an effective QFT, which makes some of its notorious problems be non-problems:
          %ul
            %li#DonoghueIntroduction
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Donoghue"}> John Donoghue
                ,
                %em Introduction to the Effective Field Theory Description of Gravity
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9512024"}> arXiv:gr-qc/9512024
                )
            %li#AtanceCortes96
              %p
                Mario Atance, Jose Luis Cortes,
                %em Effective Field Theory of pure Gravity and the Renormalization Group
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9604076"}> arXiv:hep-th/9604076
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+F.+Donoghue"}> John F. Donoghue
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum General Relativity and Effective Field Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Quantum+Gravity"} Handbook of Quantum Gravity
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.09902"} arXiv:2211.09902
          %p
            and in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbation theory
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT"} AQFT
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Romeo+Brunetti"}> Romeo Brunetti
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Katarzyna+Rejzner"} Katarzyna Rejzner
              %em Quantum gravity from the point of view of locally covariant quantum field theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1306.1058"}> arXiv:1306.1058
              )
          %p Comments on this point are also in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Distler"}> Jacques Distler
                , blog posts
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %em
                      %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/~distler/blog/archives/000639.html"} Motivation
                %li
                  %p
                    %em
                      %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/~distler/blog/archives/001255.html"} Effective field theory and gravity
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Costello"}> Kevin Costello
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Renormalization+and+Effective+Field+Theory"} Renormalization and Effective Field Theory
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alastair+Hamilton"}> Alastair Hamilton
              ,
              %em On two constructions of an effective field theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1502.05790"}> arXiv:1502.05790
              )
          %h3#for_string_theory For string theory
          %p
            Discussion of the effective field theories induced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            includes the following:
          %p
            Via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+scattering+amplitudes"} string scattering amplitudes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+Blumenhagen"}> Ralph Blumenhagen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieter+L%C3%BCst"} Dieter Lüst
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Theisen"} Stefan Theisen
              = succeed "," do
                %em String Scattering Amplitudes and Low Energy Effective Field Theory
              %em Basic Concepts of String Theory
              Part of the series Theoretical and Mathematical Physics pp 585-639 Springer 2013 (
              %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/bfm%3A978-3-642-29497-6%2F1.pdf"}> TOC pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.springer.com/gp/book/9783642294969"} publisher page
          %p
            Via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+field+theory"} string field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                R. Brustein, S.P.De Alwis,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Renormalization group equation and non-perturbative effects in string-field theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(91)90451-3"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(91)90451-3
            %li
              %p
                Brustein and K. Roland, “Space-time versus world sheet renormalization group equation in string theory,” Nucl. Phys. B372, 201 (1992) (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(92)90317-5"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(92)90317-5
                )
            %li#Sen16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Wilsonian Effective Action of Superstring Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.00459"} arXiv:1609.00459
          %p
            Discussion of possible criteria for which effective field theory do
            %em not
            arise as effective field theories of a string theory:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eran+Palti"}> Eran Palti
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Swampland: Introduction and Review
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.06239"} arXiv:1903.06239
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/landscape+of+string+theory+vacua"} landscape of string theory vacua
        .revisedby
